        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm-96b20a89c/dist/cli.js",
        "With the partial: true option (and Minimatch#match(path, true)), a path should match when it is a valid prefix of a path that the full pattern could match, including when the pattern contains **. Today patterns with a globstar wrongly report false for valid prefixes. For example minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/b/c\", { partial: true }), minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/b/c/**\", { partial: true }), minimatch(\"a\", \"a/**\", { partial: true }), minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/**/b/c/**\", { partial: true }) and minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/**\", { partial: true }) must all return true, while minimatch(\"b/a\", \"a/**\", { partial: true }) must still return false. Existing partial behavior for patterns without ** (for example \"/a/b\" against \"/*/b/x/y/z\" is true and \"/a/b/c\" is false) and makeRe(pattern, { partial: true }) must be unchanged, and non-partial matching must not loosen: minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/b/c\") stays false. Make the change in the ** path-walking logic in src/index.ts, not by post-processing results. The library is TypeScript built with npx tshy; tests run with npm test (tap, which requires 100% coverage).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npx tshy && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nAllowed changes: implementation code, and regression tests for the change (new test files, or new cases added to existing test files, in the project's own test directory and style).\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.\nDo not change how the project's checks run: leave the test and coverage configuration files (.taprc*, .nycrc*, .c8rc*, .mocharc*, jest.config.*, vitest.config.*, ava.config.*, karma.conf.*) and the test, pretest and posttest scripts and runner sections of package.json as they are.\nDo not delete or weaken existing tests: keep every existing assertion (it may move to another test file), add no skip, only or todo markers, and add no coverage-ignore pragmas. A change that does any of these is rejected at evaluation whatever else passes.",
